# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Fiesta
# Ford Fiesta Mk7 (B479, UK Mk8): announced 29 November 2016, on sale 2017 to
# July 2023, when the last Fiesta was built and the nameplate was retired from
# production. The Fiesta was the most numerous car on GB roads in 2020 (1.5m
# licensed, DfT VEH0128) and 2025 (1,368,335, SMMT Motorparc; the only model
# above one million).
#
# Colours: Magnetic Grey, Shadow Black, Frozen White, Blue Wave. The paint names
# are the actual Ford offerings with their availability years (Magnetic Grey
# 2014-2026, Shadow/absolute Black 2015-2026, Frozen White 2006-2026, Blue Wave
# 2017-2026). These are the four largest measured DVSA first-registration
# shares over the model's road years 2017-2022: grey 23.2%, black 20.0%, white
# 17.9%, blue 16.9%. Red was the next measured colour at 9.8%.
#
# Dates are staggered per colour by observed road presence. Weights total 500,
# the 2026-11-15 anchor convention for the Fiesta (provisional; a central
# rebase follows), split 23.2:20.0:17.9:16.9. Retire dates after 2026 are
# estimates for a model whose production ended in July 2023; the Fiesta was the
# GB parc leader in 2025 and a long road tail is expected.

